To make a "release", you need a working pihpsdr executable
in your pihpsdr directory. 

Then, simply do "make release". This creates the tar file

pihpsdr-GIT_VERSION.tar

where GIT_VERSION expands to the current git version.

The tar file contains the "pihpsdr" directory inside
the "release" directory, with the pihpsdr executable
added.

Recommended release flow:

- develop and merge features on master
- create a release branch named Rel-x.y at feature freeze
- accept only bug fixes and release notes updates on Rel-x.y
- create an annotated tag vX.Y.ZZ on the release branch
- run "make release" from the tagged commit to create the tarball
- publish a GitHub Release for that tag and attach the tarball
- merge or cherry-pick release fixes back to master

Version guidance:

- use the tag format v0.0.00, with a two-digit patch component
- use vX.Y.00 for a feature release
- use vX.Y.ZZ for later bug-fix releases from the same Rel-x.y branch
- non-tag builds include the nearest tag plus commit distance and hash
